<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>02 · OUT — 观察者三视角(消失/显露/丧失)与延展<span class='hero-badge'>📖 EPE Ch.2 §7</span></h1><p class='hero-sub'>OUT: Vantage Points (Disappearance vs Emergence) & Expansion</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>576</b> 个独立义项 • <b>1728</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 2 (§7 OUT OF, §8 OUTWARD, §9.3) & Chapter 4 (§2.1)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>跨越边界向外 (○→) 与三大观察者视角 (Person A / B / C Viewpoints)</b>：基本图式是主体先在容器/边界内部，随后离开内部。EPE 独创性地通过「离开房子的三种观察视角（Figures 2.4 & 2.5）」解释了为什么 OUT 能同时表达“消失”与“出现”两种相反含义。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>I managed to talk Liz out of doing more housework.</i> (将行动视为可进出的决策空间，反义：<i>talk sb into</i>) [Ch.2 (40)]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>Jo Durie is hoping her dodgy knees hold out for an emotional Wimbledon farewell.</i> (从头撑到尾的完结体) [Ch.2 (43)]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>室内观察者 Person B 视角 (Ch.2 §7.4.2 Fig.2.4)</b>：B 留在屋里看 A 走出去（<i>She's gone out</i>）→ 意味着<b>「不在场、消失、熄灭、昏迷、排除」</b>（<i>The lamp's gone out; He's out [unconscious]; bridge taken out by floods; leave/rule out</i>，对应拉丁前缀 <i>ex-</i> 如 <i>extinguish, extinct</i>）。</li><li><b>室外观察者 Person C 视角 (Ch.2 §7.4.3 Fig.2.5)</b>：C 站在屋外看 A 走出来（<i>She's come out</i>）→ 意味着<b>「从隐藏变为公开、显露、查明、出版」</b>（<i>bring differences out in the open; figure/work/reason it out; My book is out</i>，对应拉丁 <i>ex-plain</i> 展平使可见）。</li><li><b>当事人 Person A 视角 (Ch.2 §7.4.4) & 延展完结体 (§7.3)</b>：从“拥有某物的状态空间”走出来即<b>丧失/耗尽</b>（<i>run out of time; cheat sb out of money</i>）；像融化的黄油摊开或卷轴展开至尽头即<b>延展与坚持到底</b>（<i>spread/roll/fill out; fight it out; knees hold out</i>）。</li></ul></div></div></details>

